        "date": "2026-11-26T16:00:38Z"
      },
      "message": "feat(tools): lathe tool assemblies - nose-centre tip, orientation and clearance\n\nA turning holder or boring bar with its insert (and adapters) resolves\nto the nose centre as the tip of the turning frame, the derived\nLinuxCNC orientation (1-8), the nose radius and the seat and insert\nvalues, and one LatheClearance over all non-insert bodies. The spindle\nchain is shared through tool_assembly::placed. Refusals are named:\nfit, orientation, no nose radius, a revolved body, a body past the\ncutting lines near the nose, and the clearance errors on the whole\nstack.\n\nRefs #3643\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
